6. Full Legal Case Specification
6.1 Legal Case Schema
The legal case schema defines the structure of a legal case deposit.

It has the following fields:

case_id. A string. Required.

case_name. A string. Required.

citation. A string. Required.

court. A string. Required.

date_decided. A string in ISO8601 format. Required.

jurisdiction. A string. Required.

subject_matter. An array of strings. Required.

holding. An object. Required. It contains statement and rule_type.

key_phrases. An array of strings. Optional.

summary. A string. Required.

precedents_established. An array of precedent objects. Optional.

precedents_followed. An array of precedent objects. Optional.

precedents_distinguished. An array of precedent objects. Optional.

precedents_overruled. An array of precedent objects. Optional.

overruled_by. An array of precedent objects. Optional.

related_cases. An array of case relations. Optional.

judges. An array of judge objects. Optional.

parties. An array of party objects. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each precedent object has:

precedent_id. A string.

case_reference. A string.

precedent_type. An enum. The values are followed, distinguished, overruled, doubted, criticised, applied, considered, other.

precedent_strength. An enum. The values are binding, persuasive, not_assessed.

precedent_reason. A string. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each case relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_case_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_subject, related, distinguished, overruled, affirmed, reversed, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

Each judge object has:

judge_id. A string.

judge_name. A string.

judge_role. An enum. The values are presiding, concurring, dissenting, other.

Each party object has:

party_id. A string.

party_name. A string.

party_role. An enum. The values are plaintiff, defendant, appellant, respondent, other.

