7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Legal Case
function createLegalCase(legalCase, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the case against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. Generate a case ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 5. Insert the legal case.

Step 6. Insert the precedent records, the case relations, the judges, and the parties.

Step 7. Insert the work link if present.

Step 8. Insert the provenance.

Step 9. Insert the moderation record.

Step 10. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 11. Return the case_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Legal Case
function readLegalCase(caseId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the case. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the precedents, the case relations, the judges, the parties, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Legal Case
function updateLegalCase(caseId, legalCase, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing case. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new case.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the case_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Legal Case
function deleteLegalCase(caseId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing case. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the case_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Legal Cases
function queryLegalCases(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching cases.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the cases, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Legal Cases
function aggregateLegalCases(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching cases.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the cases and the count.

7.8 Export Legal Case
function exportLegalCase(caseId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each case, call createLegalCase.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching cases.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per case. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Legal Case
function moderateLegalCase(caseId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing case. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the case_id and the status.

